{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/635560-help-me-house-rule-creation-system","id":635560,"title":"Help me house-rule creation system","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-22T03:39:59-07:00","id":635560,"title":"Help me house-rule creation system","content":"Hi folks.<br /> <br /> Need you help with developing a character creation system that take character age into account. I had a quick look at Ars Magica 5th edition and they have sections of age defined in a way i like (early childehood, apprenticeship etc) with more xp for older characters. Now ofc an older character should have more XP but also drawbacks.<br /> <br /> Basicly a system that makes a diffrence between a character that is 40 years old and someone who is in their teens. This is before they turn supernatural (Embrace, First change, Awaken etc)<br /> Also their should be some baseline and diffrence for someone who has been supernatural longer than others.<br /> <br /> There is a destinction between supers in game (Age, Rank, Arete etc) but even among Neonates thair is significant diffrence.<br /> <br /> If we focus on Vampire for a while i feel there should a diffrence between for example a Ventrue and a Gangrel. The Clans should have some form of template that defines the character from which clan he/she chooses. For example a Ventrue should have a few more dots because he/she spent longer time as a fledgling before being released. Also stuff like Camarilla Lore and Clan lore. Of course you can always buck the clan stereotypes but now i'm talking about steroetype characters.<br /> <br /> Same goes for the Traditions. An Order of Hermes usually have diffrent traits than a Cultist or a Verbena.<br /> <br /> So, what kind of system could one build with this? 1 Freebie per 5 years over 10 years old (up till embrace, first change etc)? With another few freebies depending on how long the character have been supernatural?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T05:14:52-07:00","id":635619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/635560-help-me-house-rule-creation-system#post635560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now ofc an older character should have more XP but also drawbacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the first part of this deserves some examination as an assumption (but it would be a bit threadcrapy to focus on that), but the last part is the crux of this whole endeavor.<br /> <br /> What you intend for the drawbacks to be needs to be decided well before figuring out what the numbers for the bonuses should be. The drawbacks have to be significant enough that there's a reason you might want to make a younger character. If being young doesn't get you a bunch of freebies... what does it get you?<br /> <br /> Otherwise the system is going to give all the incentive to making as old of characters as the ST allows you to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T05:41:05-07:00","id":635684,"title":"","content":"I think this is a very troublesome approach. Not only for the reasons Heavy Arms allready listed (old chars or specific factions usually getting the better end of the bargain in such a deal), but also because it gets very complicated, very fast. New players will often be confused by such extensive rules as you desire them, more experienced players may be annyoed by some details of your homerules or feel constricted because the char they wanted to play get's a huge comparative statnerf using the system. So it basically only works with a rather limited amount of players. I personally don't think there are many good awnsers as it comes to possible drawbacks. Just arbitrarily slapping on certain flaws (derangements, enemies, low humanity) is just meh and restrictive as far as char background goes.<br /> <br /> <br /> I personally think that if you wish to give out more diversified stats you should probably &quot;wing it&quot; in the prep phase of a campaign. Talk to your players and let them give you a background story rather than any sheet. Then give out bonus stats before they do the normal char gen on top of it as you see fit. Naturally older chars need to have a far more extended background write up which probably offers quite a few hooks for you as ST to use (possibly against them). This basically rewards the player for writing more extensive backgrounds and the &quot;bonus&quot; points you give out can also allready include certain flaws or negative backgrounds based on their backstory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T09:31:45-07:00","id":635922,"title":"","content":"This is the reason why people in CoC tend to be way older then in any other game :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T11:34:59-07:00","id":636107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/635560-help-me-house-rule-creation-system?p=635922#post635922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the reason why people in CoC tend to be way older then in any other game :P</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, being a young and physically powerful human only really helps you run away faster in CoC. Most Mythos beasts don't care a whit if you are an Olympic sharpshooter or world-class strongman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T14:54:45-07:00","id":636290,"title":"","content":"When it comes to humans, I don't necessarily know if older humans should have more points than younger ones. Many extremely accomplished people hit their peak at a young age and many people have no skills when they are young and get old and still don't have any skills. Though it is a common trope for supernatural beings to get more powerful with age, especially since many of them don't physically decline as they get older. <br /> <br /> If you have a system which provides extra points for greater age, everybody will want to be older, and you'll end up having to limit age at some point - so just give out that many freebie points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T15:31:59-07:00","id":636331,"title":"","content":"For what you seems to want, I'd say you need some character templates done. Just that. Take each clan, see what you think the clan should have, and them put it there, already taking it out from the points fro Character Creation. A simple way to do that is to ascribe previously some Flaws to each clan and buy something for each with the points taken from the Flaws. When handling the sheet to your players, say that the character creation process will run normally, and what's already on the sheet are irremovable extras.<br /> <br /> You decide if the Flaws taken count or not for the limit. Not counting could work for the Age template.<br /> <br /> On another thought, in the Age you could not eve make a Template, but instead tie not the Freebies, but the FLAWS to the character age. You create some age categories, and for each one you charge a maximum on Flaws. That way every character have the same amount of points, but older characters can get both more juice and more problems. All that without messing too much with character balance. And be prepared for a lot of older characters, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T16:34:52-07:00","id":636426,"title":"","content":"Simple: allow players to exchange 1 Attribute point for 3 Ability points for every 5 (10?) years over their prime age (which is very culture/lifestyle dependent).<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T21:58:16-07:00","id":875272,"title":"","content":"With me, i gave mortals (which would include garou/Fera kinfolk, Vampire's ghouls and such, +2 dots of skills and knowledges for every decade they started over 25 years of age. But capped it at putting +1 into any one skill/knowledge Per decade you were (so a 55 yr old got +6 dots, but could put only 3 into any one skill/knowledge).. At 65 and over, each 5 years, Dropped your physical and mental attributes by 1 point (PC choice which was lost).. So a 75 yr old would have 3 dots missing from both..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}